        "value": "Wax-tree berries (haze no mi) = 3,500,000 kin. Flush at the value-band top, so a top-level 國産 (national products) entry alongside the farm animals; the 益金 column to its left records the profit on it. The first glyph is 櫨 (wax tree), not 樟 (camphor): it carries the 虍 tiger-top and 皿 base of 盧 and matches the well-inked 櫨實 printed for Kumamoto (upper_p183_left), while 樟's symmetric 立 top and 早 descender are absent. MASTER's 樟實 / 'camphor' is a misread. MASTER also writes 拾 where the print uses a plain 十 (same value)."
